The earlier [Archive and prerequisite run](results/cloud-archive-prerequisites-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) executed **161 checks: 155 passed and six failed**, with zero skips, on the overlay based on `b15d166`; its 779-file census stayed stable and 357 source snapshots are backed up locally. Acquisition of the pinned bsdtar EXE/DLL pair and other development inputs succeeded, and one separate original `--version` smoke passed. This failed source epoch remains preserved.

The [later Archive finite experiment](results/cloud-archive-aes-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **161/161 checks with zero failures or skips** after the literal-path correction. Run `38808918976` tested the composed overlay on actual Git merge `7d5bde3`, distinct from PR head `aeb62e6`; its 779-file census remained stable. The path diagnostics confirm real short-name/long-name aliases while the metadata checks pass. All 389 evidence files, including 357 source snapshots, remain in the verified local backup; the public capsule retains all non-source evidence and the omitted snapshots' identities. Original prerequisites, the separate one-process bsdtar smoke and the post-run source check also passed. Production installation remains false; browser acceptance, the full Archive scope and the full ten-application suite remain pending.

The [full hosted replay](results/cloud-full-suite-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) now records 1,042 checks: 1,024 passed, 18 failed and zero skipped, with 770 stable source identities and 348 backed-up active snapshots. It used actual merge `abcac0b2` and the explicit three-source paired-oracle test overlay. The failures concern the Editor Git root observer and Sync WebDAV short Windows root paths. The later focused experiment below verifies candidate corrections, which were subsequently integrated; the failed record does not replace historical receipts or establish current full-suite acceptance.

The [focused Windows path experiment](results/cloud-windows-path-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **47/47 finite Editor Git and Sync WebDAV checks with zero skips** on actual tested merge `93b5dbe7`, separate from PR head `b0cdb550`. It uses an explicit three-target derivative: one Sync runtime correction, one Editor path-observer correction and one new regression file. A genuine hosted Windows short-root alias was observed; the 772-file composed census and separate three-target postcheck stayed exact. All 350 active source snapshots remain in the verified complete local backup. The exact three reviewed sources were subsequently [installed in the local application source](results/windows-path-installed-20261015/installation-receipt.json), with verified before/after bytes. The subsequent [hosted committed-source check](results/cloud-windows-path-installed-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes 47/47 with zero skips on merge `4a69ae1f`, authenticates all 350 eligible active sources against Git and passes the separate source postcheck. A fresh full suite remains pending; the failed 1,042-check record is unchanged.

The [hosted Flow/Vault browser run](results/cloud-flow-vault-browser-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **12/12 finite Chromium cases**, with zero failures, skips or retries, on unmodified tested merge `f138ee5a`, separate from PR head `dc0fce2b`. It verifies three real downloads byte for byte and records twelve screenshots, six real-response timing holds and two explicitly programmatic probes of disabled Flow controls; the latter are not ordinary user typing. All 326 captured source identities stayed exact and their snapshots remain in the verified complete local backup. The public capsule retains every non-source artifact file, the raw downloads and viewable PNG evidence. No original product runs occurred. These results do not establish Archive browser, full-suite, browser-matrix, full-product or comparative acceptance; counts from different campaigns are not added.
