{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Fix Windows paths, preserve the full-suite pass and extend hosted acceptance",
  "body": "Windows short-root paths caused18 failures in the implemented suite. This branch integrates the reviewed Sync root correction, Editor path observer and six real Windows regressions. The [integrated full-suite run](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38816488464) passes1048/1048 with zero failures or skips; two later full repeats also pass. Each uses an explicit three-source paired-bsdtar test-loader overlay, with application runtime bytes authenticated against Git, stable source inventories, a separate postcheck and verified recoverable local evidence. Historical937/737 and the failed1042/18 receipts are preserved unchanged.\n\nThe [current Flow/Vault browser study](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38814582306) passes12 real Chromium scenarios, with three byte-exact downloads and zero retries/skips. Six actual-response holds and two programmatic disabled-control probes are disclosed. The public evidence includes raw downloads and viewable screenshots; all source snapshots remain in verified portable local backups.\n\nThe delivery audit found80 missing declared historical carriers. This branch restores exactly those reviewed files and admits eleven otherwise excluded source snapshots through one fixed path/byte/SHA policy bound to the original manifests. Unknown paths remain refused. Prior proof epochs and160-file/16MiB reader bounds are preserved;76 focused publication controls are authored for hosted execution. The audit retains unresolved schemas and makes no exhaustive coverage claim. Full publication must pass before the two excluded derived metadata files are imported.\n\nArchive's21-target AES/timestamp derivative previously passed161 finite checks and remains uninstalled. New isolated hosted workflows exercise six real Archive browser scenarios and Vault Empty Recycle Bin across the fixed45-file Vault roster, including27 new authored groups and four separately counted released KeePass library operations. These workflows have bounded evidence capture and independent source postchecks. Their first actual results are pending; no new feature acceptance is preclaimed.\n\nAll ten complete replacements, every documented original feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain unfinished. See [CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) and [STATUS.json](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/products/rea-studio/STATUS.json) for exact evidence and limits. No local product tests/builds or paid resources were used for this recovery."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Archive AES and Notes task editing; verify 1,100 implemented checks",
  "body": "Archive gains AES 7Z, encrypted-header handling and native Windows timestamps. Notes gains saved-note conversion to and from to-dos, completion and reopening, due dates and filters, with draft, JEX and resource retention. Both integrations install exact independently reviewed sources with recoverable before/after journals and pushed pre-installation Git tags.\n\nThe committed Notes integration passes 92/92 groups across all 17 fixed test files and eight real Chromium cases in run38917424088 on head362bda05. Both jobs authenticate all 32 Notes files, eight application target pins and 27 dependencies, with separate source postchecks. The finite job records 20 released Joplin helper comparisons separately. Browser evidence includes four genuine response holds, two byte-exact downloads, one actual conflict and explicit retry, and eight complete owned cleanups. Complete 449-file and 495-file local backups are readable; exact public portable ZIPs retain every uploaded byte. The first CRLF backup-reader failure and both reader versions are retained without claiming a product rerun.\n\nThe full implemented suite passes 1,100/1,100 with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos in run38917433182, testing actual merge6c3c4eca for branch head362bda05. All 796 census identities remain stable; 369 eligible sources match Git and exactly three Archive oracle-test loader/helper targets are composed. Application runtime and Notes have no overlays. All five same-attempt prerequisites and the separate oracle-source postcheck pass. Seven eligible Notes after-images, all 17 Notes test files, 23 task groups and 20 separate helper comparisons are authenticated within this run. The Notes README is outside the full-suite census and is authenticated by the focused jobs. The complete 429-file local backup and exact public artifact ZIP retain all 372 active snapshots; all other 57 uploaded roles are directly retained too. Focused and full-suite counts are never added together.\n\nArchive's corrected committed-source run38911241646 separately passes 161 selected checks and six real Chromium scenarios. All 62 Archive files and 21 target pins match Git. Exact public portable ZIPs and 470-file/474-file readable local backups retain every artifact member. The extra three-group bounds repeat overlaps the 161 selection. Its test-only correction removes a probabilistic malformed-input fixture while retaining the rejection assertion; runtime parsing and historical receipts remain unchanged. Earlier 1,077-group full-suite results keep their original source attribution.\n\nPublication run38915607121 previously passed 164 controls, both root phases, 953 syntax checks and stable 27,911-file payload verification. Only its two exact generated metadata files were imported incc7a583. The first new 208-control attempt38917432854 stopped in its first named migration check: zero controls passed and zero root phases started. Two historical Notes IDs are strings, while the reader incorrectly required numbers. Commitc15dd78 corrects only those two strict assertions and their existing module/producer pins, retaining all 208 controls, read limits, envelope tables and historical records. All 85 uploaded failure files, the complete original ZIP and 56 decoded Notes envelope sources are preserved. Fresh hosted publication acceptance of the changed payload is pending; no new metadata has been imported. The diagnostic delivery audit retains 976 unresolved declarations, zero known missing carriers and no exhaustive-coverage claim.\n\nVault Empty Recycle Bin experiment38903252563 separately passes 233 checks and four KeePass library comparisons using the exact original whole-second serialization rule. It remains uninstalled. Direct New to-do creation is a separate source proposal awaiting cloud tests; its late-refresh status race was found and corrected during independent review.\n\nTests and builds run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work remains lightweight authoring, orchestration and recoverable backup verification. No paid resources or billing changes. [Hosted verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) retain exact sources, failures and comparison limits. All ten complete replacements, every documented feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain open."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Fix Windows paths and extend verified Archive, Vault and Notes workflows",
  "body": "Windows short-root paths caused 18 failures in the implemented suite. This branch integrates the reviewed Sync root correction, Editor observer and real Windows regressions. The latest [full hosted replay](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38826470337) passes all 1,048 implemented checks with zero failures or skips. The actual tested merge and the three-source oracle-test overlay are explicit; application runtime bytes match Git, source inventories are stable, separate postchecks pass and complete readable local backups are verified. Historical 937/737 and all failed attempts remain unchanged.\n\n[Archive browser acceptance](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38826463567) passes six real Chromium cases, creating three archives and restoring five files with exact bytes. The 21-target Archive derivative remains experimental and uninstalled. The [Flow/Vault browser follow-up](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38826470332) passes twelve cases with three exact downloads and verified request/context/server cleanup in every case. This does not establish the precise cause of the earlier timeout or a broader reliability improvement.\n\nExactly 80 missing historical carriers are restored under a closed path/byte/SHA policy. Eleven otherwise excluded source snapshots have explicit fixed identities; unknown paths remain refused. A broken documentation link and historical requirement-evidence reads are corrected without rewriting registries, capability gates or historical behavioral receipts. The new reader keeps its 160-file/16MiB bounds and has 92 authored integrity controls; hosted final publication acceptance is pending. The delivery diagnostic still records unresolved schemas and makes no exhaustive-coverage claim. Derived metadata is imported only after full publication validation.\n\nIsolated hosted experiments extend Vault Empty Recycle Bin and Notes conversion/completion, due dates and filtering. Their exact source bundles, original-source comparisons, complete current-product test rosters and separate source postchecks must pass before installation. New feature acceptance is not preclaimed. The Archive, Vault and Notes experiments need later production integration and broader checks.\n\nAll ten complete replacements, every documented original feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain unfinished. [CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) gives the evidence and limits. All product execution uses standard GitHub-hosted Windows; local work is limited to authoring, orchestration and verified recoverable backups. No paid resources or billing changes."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Windows path fixes and resume hosted REA verification",
  "body": "An interrupted verification left reviewed application changes without current acceptance. This branch adds pinned GitHub-hosted Windows execution, streamed and bounded evidence, separate source postchecks, and verified portable local backups. It integrates the exact reviewed Sync canonical-root correction, Editor physical-path test observer and six-case Windows regression file. Before/after source copies and the actual local source-installation receipt are retained. The [hosted committed-source check](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38816488430) subsequently passed47/47 with a separate postcheck and all350 active source images authenticated to Git; a new full suite remains required.\n\nThe [first full replay](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38810678336) failed18 of1,042 checks with zero skips: one Editor observer and17 Sync cases exposed Windows short/canonical path handling. The subsequent [focused derivative](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38814327316) passed47/47 with a real Windows8.3 alias and an independent source postcheck. That experiment retains its own source epoch and does not become an integrated full-suite certificate. Its three reviewed source images are now committed; the focused workflow explicitly distinguishes clean committed after-images from its earlier temporary composition.\n\n[Real Chromium Flow/Vault execution](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38814582306) passed12 declared cases without skips or retries, verified three downloads byte for byte and recorded12 screenshots. Six real-response timing holds and two explicitly programmatic probes of disabled controls are disclosed; the latter are not ordinary typing. All326 active snapshots and raw evidence have a verified readable local backup. The public capsule preserves every non-source artifact file and viewable PNGs. The separate Flow/Vault282 campaign and synthetic collector controls retain their own immutable epochs.\n\nThe [Archive AES/timestamp derivative](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38808918976) passed161 finite checks with zero skips on an explicit21-target composition. It remains uninstalled pending source-proof integration, a new full suite and browser acceptance. Authenticated original-tool acquisition and a separate bsdtar version smoke are prerequisite evidence; their counts are not added to product comparisons.\n\nHistorical937/737 and other earlier receipts remain unchanged. Narrow historical readers now preserve Git-safe delivery of exact nested.git fixture bytes, and source controls reject unknown identities. The latest [publication replay](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38817683491) passed70 source controls, then found another historical .local proof carrier omitted from Git. Its complete uploaded evidence is backed up, and a systematic hosted delivery census is being prepared to identify remaining omissions. Full publication integrity must pass on the final payload revision before the two excluded derived publication records are imported. All ten products remain incomplete against the requested every-documented-feature and comparative-quality scope; no universal superiority or completion is claimed.\n\nEvidence and limits: [CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md)."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Archive AES and Notes task editing; verify 1,100 implemented checks",
  "body": "Archive gains AES 7Z, encrypted-header handling and native Windows timestamps. Notes gains saved-note conversion to and from to-dos, completion and reopening, due dates and filters, with draft, JEX and resource retention. Both integrations install exact independently reviewed sources with recoverable before/after journals and pushed pre-installation Git tags.\n\nThe committed Notes integration passes 92/92 groups across all 17 fixed test files and eight real Chromium cases in run38917424088 on head362bda05. Both jobs authenticate all 32 Notes files, eight application target pins and 27 dependencies, with separate source postchecks. The finite job records 20 released Joplin helper comparisons separately. Browser evidence includes four genuine response holds, two byte-exact downloads, one actual conflict and explicit retry, and eight complete owned cleanups. Complete 449-file and 495-file local backups are readable; exact public portable ZIPs retain every uploaded byte. The first CRLF backup-reader failure and both reader versions are retained without claiming a product rerun.\n\nThe full implemented suite passes 1,100/1,100 with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos in run38917433182, testing actual merge6c3c4eca for branch head362bda05. All 796 census identities remain stable; 369 eligible sources match Git and exactly three Archive oracle-test loader/helper targets are composed. Application runtime and Notes have no overlays. All five same-attempt prerequisites and the separate oracle-source postcheck pass. Seven eligible Notes after-images, all 17 Notes test files, 23 task groups and 20 separate helper comparisons are authenticated within this run. The Notes README is outside the full-suite census and is authenticated by the focused jobs. The complete 429-file local backup and exact public artifact ZIP retain all 372 active snapshots; all other 57 uploaded roles are directly retained too. Focused and full-suite counts are never added together.\n\nArchive's corrected committed-source run38911241646 separately passes 161 selected checks and six real Chromium scenarios. All 62 Archive files and 21 target pins match Git. Exact public portable ZIPs and 470-file/474-file readable local backups retain every artifact member. The extra three-group bounds repeat overlaps the 161 selection. Its test-only correction removes a probabilistic malformed-input fixture while retaining the rejection assertion; runtime parsing and historical receipts remain unchanged. Earlier 1,077-group full-suite results keep their original source attribution. A separate automatic c15 repeat also passes 1,100/1,100 with complete 429-file readable evidence; it is not added to the earlier count.\n\nPublication verification now passes all 208 source controls, both root write/recheck phases and 959 syntax checks. Run38922041634 first verifies exact25b payload; its complete 92-file artifact, complete ZIP, all 56 decoded Notes proof sources, raw API/log evidence and independent source/byte reviews are published. The added preservation files and documentation then receive their own successful validation in run38923831870 on d8c80d1 / actual merge38d768cf. That 28,540-file / 1,351,008,568-byte payload stays stable. Only its two exact derived metadata files are imported and committed in a1fa90c, with readable before/after backups and an independently reviewed importer that requires the actual clean HEAD/tree, completed raw API/artifact digest, all 208 rows, both phases and the exact 56-source envelope. No earlier receipt is reused for a changed payload.\n\nBoth publication failures remain intact: the first stopped before any control passed because two historical IDs were checked as numbers instead of exact strings; the second passed 121 controls before an older positive expectation contradicted the already-correct historical followup-reader route. The narrow corrections preserve every historical record, all 208 control groups, unknown-identity rejections and read limits, and add an explicit current-reader assertion. They change no application runtime. The separate delivery diagnostic retains 980 unresolved declarations and zero known missing carriers, with no exhaustive-coverage claim.\n\nVault Empty Recycle Bin experiment38903252563 separately passes 233 checks and four KeePass library comparisons using the exact original whole-second serialization rule. It remains uninstalled. Direct New to-do creation is now a separately committed source experiment in b635c33. Independently reviewed exact after-images are composed only inside an ephemeral hosted checkout; the installed 32-file Notes application stays unchanged. Actual run38926216286 failed: 107 of 111 selected groups and seven of eight browser cases passed, with zero skips. Three older notebook-trash cases expose an overly broad Save busy guard; two new comparisons incorrectly mix initial and normalized metadata epochs. Strict baseline and narrow concurrency corrections are independently source-reviewed and await a separate frozen proposal and fresh hosted acceptance. Both complete artifacts retain all 1,110 uploaded members; the failed results remain failed. Its late-refresh status race was found and corrected during source review. Original comparisons remain narrow helpers and command arguments; original desktop provisional persistence and GUI are not executed.\n\nTests and builds run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work remains lightweight authoring, orchestration and recoverable backup verification. No paid resources or billing changes. [Hosted verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) retain exact sources, failures and comparison limits. All ten complete replacements, every documented feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain open."
}
