{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Archive AES and timestamps, extend Notes and Vault workflows",
  "body": "Archive gains the reviewed AES 7Z, encrypted-header and native Windows source timestamp implementation. Its 21 exact source targets are installed, with a recoverable before/after journal and preserved pre-installation Git tag. All 62 Archive files are authenticated against Git before and after separate finite/browser jobs. Historical bundles and experimental receipts retain their original source identities and uninstalled declarations.\n\nThe broader suite exposed a probabilistic malformed-input test: dropping the first property byte can accidentally describe another valid direct-key sequence, reaching CRC refusal. The correction truncates the final byte, preserves the exact properties-refusal assertion and adds deterministic EF/FE counterexamples. Runtime parsing is unchanged. A closed single-test transition keeps both source epochs readable; the targeted three-group phase repeats part of finite161 and is never counted as additional coverage.\n\nVerified evidence:\n\n- Installed Archive run38905573441 passes161 selected checks and six real Chromium cases on committed5ff, with three archives, five byte-exact restored files and complete466/471-file backups. The first broader5ff run fails1076/1077; a later6af repeat passes1077 with the same predecessor fixture. Neither accepts the new correction. Fresh corrected-source run38911241646 and full38911252546 are pending.\n- Notes run38903252258 passes92 checks across17 files and20 separate Joplin helper comparisons. Its first real-browser run38908759571 passes8/8 with four genuine response holds, a real HTTP400 conflict/retry, two actual downloads and eight complete cleanups. All467 artifact files and383 source snapshots are retained in the public portable capsule and readable local backup. Notes remains an eight-target uninstalled experiment.\n- Vault Empty Recycle Bin run38903252563 passes233 checks and four separate actual KeePass library operations/comparisons, using the authenticated original whole-second serialization rule. Raw observations remain intact; this feature remains uninstalled.\n\nPublication recovery restores80 exact historical carriers through a closed identity policy. The corrected historical pending-string reader passes156 controls, both root phases and final payload stability on exact2e,6af andf61 payloads. The new named-test transition adds eight controls, for164 planned current controls; run38911251888 must validate the new payload before either derived metadata file is imported. Reader/artifact bounds and earlier checks remain intact. The delivery diagnostic still reports unresolved schemas and makes no exhaustive coverage claim.\n\nAll product/build/browser execution uses standard GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work is source authoring, orchestration and verified recoverable backups. No paid resources or billing changes. [CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) gives exact scopes. All ten complete replacements, every documented feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain unfinished."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Archive AES and Notes task editing; verify 1,100 implemented checks",
  "body": "Archive gains AES 7Z, encrypted-header handling and native Windows timestamps. Notes gains saved-note conversion to and from to-dos, completion and reopening, due dates and filters, with draft, JEX and resource retention. Both integrations install exact independently reviewed sources with recoverable before/after journals and pushed pre-installation Git tags.\n\nThe committed Notes integration passes 92/92 groups across all 17 fixed test files and eight real Chromium cases in run38917424088 on head362bda05. Both jobs authenticate all 32 Notes files, eight application target pins and 27 dependencies, with separate source postchecks. The finite job records 20 released Joplin helper comparisons separately. Browser evidence includes four genuine response holds, two byte-exact downloads, one actual conflict and explicit retry, and eight complete owned cleanups. Complete 449-file and 495-file local backups are readable; exact public portable ZIPs retain every uploaded byte. The first CRLF backup-reader failure and both reader versions are retained without claiming a product rerun.\n\nThe full implemented suite passes 1,100/1,100 with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos in run38917433182, testing actual merge6c3c4eca for branch head362bda05. All 796 census identities remain stable; 369 eligible sources match Git and exactly three Archive oracle-test loader/helper targets are composed. Application runtime and Notes have no overlays. All five same-attempt prerequisites and the separate oracle-source postcheck pass. Seven eligible Notes after-images, all 17 Notes test files, 23 task groups and 20 separate helper comparisons are authenticated within this run. The Notes README is outside the full-suite census and is authenticated by the focused jobs. The complete 429-file local backup and exact public artifact ZIP retain all 372 active snapshots; all other 57 uploaded roles are directly retained too. Focused and full-suite counts are never added together.\n\nArchive's corrected committed-source run38911241646 separately passes 161 selected checks and six real Chromium scenarios. All 62 Archive files and 21 target pins match Git. Exact public portable ZIPs and 470-file/474-file readable local backups retain every artifact member. The extra three-group bounds repeat overlaps the 161 selection. Its test-only correction removes a probabilistic malformed-input fixture while retaining the rejection assertion; runtime parsing and historical receipts remain unchanged. Earlier 1,077-group full-suite results keep their original source attribution. A separate automatic c15 repeat also passes 1,100/1,100 with complete 429-file readable evidence; it is not added to the earlier count.\n\nPublication verification now passes all 208 source controls, both root write/recheck phases and 959 syntax checks. Run38922041634 first verifies exact25b payload; its complete 92-file artifact, complete ZIP, all 56 decoded Notes proof sources, raw API/log evidence and independent source/byte reviews are published. The added preservation files and documentation then receive their own successful validation in run38923831870 on d8c80d1 / actual merge38d768cf. That 28,540-file / 1,351,008,568-byte payload stays stable. Only its two exact derived metadata files are imported and committed in a1fa90c, with readable before/after backups and an independently reviewed importer that requires the actual clean HEAD/tree, completed raw API/artifact digest, all 208 rows, both phases and the exact 56-source envelope. No earlier receipt is reused for a changed payload.\n\nBoth publication failures remain intact: the first stopped before any control passed because two historical IDs were checked as numbers instead of exact strings; the second passed 121 controls before an older positive expectation contradicted the already-correct historical followup-reader route. The narrow corrections preserve every historical record, all 208 control groups, unknown-identity rejections and read limits, and add an explicit current-reader assertion. They change no application runtime. The separate delivery diagnostic retains 980 unresolved declarations and zero known missing carriers, with no exhaustive-coverage claim.\n\nVault Empty Recycle Bin experiment38903252563 separately passes 233 checks and four KeePass library comparisons using the exact original whole-second serialization rule. It remains uninstalled. Direct New to-do creation is now a separately committed source experiment in b635c33. Independently reviewed exact after-images are composed only inside an ephemeral hosted checkout; the installed 32-file Notes application stays unchanged. Run38926216286 is testing 111 selected groups and eight real Chromium scenarios. These counts are planned gates while results are pending. Its late-refresh status race was found and corrected during source review. Original comparisons remain narrow helpers and command arguments; original desktop provisional persistence and GUI are not executed.\n\nTests and builds run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work remains lightweight authoring, orchestration and recoverable backup verification. No paid resources or billing changes. [Hosted verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) retain exact sources, failures and comparison limits. All ten complete replacements, every documented feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain open."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Archive AES and Notes task editing; extend Vault recovery",
  "body": "Archive gains AES 7Z, encrypted-header handling and native Windows timestamps. Notes gains saved-note conversion to/from to-dos, completion/reopening, due metadata and filters while preserving drafts, JEX records and resources. Both integrations install exact independently reviewed source images with recoverable before/after journals and pushed pre-installation Git tags.\n\nArchive's corrected committed-source run38911241646 passes161 selected checks and six real Chromium scenarios. All62 Archive files/21 target pins match Git; exact public portable ZIPs and470/474-file readable local backups retain every artifact member. A separately repeated three-group bounds phase overlaps161 and adds no coverage count. The test-only correction removes a probabilistic malformed-input fixture while retaining its rejection assertion; AES runtime parsing and historical receipts are unchanged.\n\nThe pre-Notes-integration full suite passes1077/1077 with zero failures/skips in run38911252546, tested mergeb7bb3010/head016. All789 census identities stay stable;363 eligible sources match Git and three oracle-test loader/helper sources are explicitly composed. Runtime sources are not overlaid. All five same-attempt prerequisites and the independent source postcheck pass. Complete423-file local evidence includes366 active snapshots; every other57 uploaded artifact role and omitted-source identities remain public. This result is not rebound to the newly changed Notes source.\n\nNotes integration at362bda0 copies eight application targets and26 proof/tooling/preservation files. The actual journal retains12 before/34 after readable local source copies, public before aliases and the exactcc7 recovery tag. Earlier experimental run38903252258 passes92 groups/17 files and20 separate Joplin helper comparisons. Browser38908759571 passes8/8 with four real response holds, a genuine conflict/retry, two downloads and eight complete cleanups; its complete467-file artifact remains portable publicly and readable locally. New installed run38917424088 is in progress and must supply its own finite/browser/source-postcheck evidence. The two historical experiment workflows retire automatic triggers while preserving strict manual replay at their historical revisions.\n\nVault Empty Recycle Bin experiment38903252563 separately passes233 checks and four KeePass library operations/comparisons using the exact original whole-second serialization rule. It remains uninstalled.\n\nPublication run38915607121 passes164 controls, both root phases,953 syntax checks and stable27,911-file payload verification. Only its exact two generated metadata files were imported incc7a583; a subsequent cc7 replay confirms the same payload and canonical manifest. Notes adds44 source controls, retaining all164 earlier controls for208 planned checks and a bounded56-source envelope under unchanged artifact limits. Fresh208 publication and the new full-suite epoch remain pending. The delivery diagnostic retains969 unresolved declarations and no complete-coverage claim.\n\nProduct tests/builds run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work is source authoring, orchestration and readable backup verification. No paid resources or billing changes. [Hosted verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) preserve exact source/measurement boundaries. All ten complete replacements, every documented feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain open."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Archive AES and timestamps, extend Notes and Vault workflows",
  "body": "Archive gains AES 7Z, encrypted-header handling and native Windows source timestamps. Its 21 reviewed source targets are installed with a recoverable before/after journal and pre-installation Git tag. The corrected committed-source run38911241646 passes all161 selected checks and six real Chromium scenarios; all62 Archive files and21 after pins match Git before and after. The separate targeted three-group repeat overlaps the161 selection. Public exact portable ZIPs and readable470/474-file local backups retain every uploaded artifact member.\n\nThe broader suite exposed a probabilistic malformed-input fixture: dropping the first property byte can describe another valid direct-key sequence. The reviewed correction truncates the final byte, retains the exact properties-refusal assertion and adds deterministic EF/FE counterexamples. AES runtime parsing, historical bundles, receipts and the installation journal remain unchanged.\n\nThe corrected full implemented suite now passes1077/1077 with zero failures/skips in run38911252546, on tested mergeb7bb3010 for head016ecd17. All789 census identities stay stable;363 eligible sources match Git and exactly three oracle-test loader/helper sources are composed. Application runtime is not overlaid. The corrected test is authenticated in the executed selection, Git baseline and snapshot. All five same-attempt prerequisites and the independent postcheck pass. The423-file readable backup includes all366 active snapshots; the public capsule preserves all57 other artifact roles, raw API/log evidence and exact omitted source identities. Earlier failed and predecessor-pass results remain separate.\n\nOther bounded progress:\n\n- Notes run38903252258 passes92 checks across17 files and20 separate released-Joplin helper comparisons. Browser run38908759571 passes8/8 with four genuine response holds, a real revision conflict/retry, two actual downloads and eight complete cleanups. All467 uploaded files are locally readable and preserved in the public portable capsule. Exact source integration and new committed-source tooling are independently reviewed work in progress; Notes remains uninstalled in this commit.\n- Vault Empty Recycle Bin run38903252563 passes233 checks and four separately counted KeePass library operations/comparisons, using the exact original whole-second serialization rule. This feature remains experimental.\n\nPublication run38911251888 passes all164 controls, both root phases,953 syntax checks and a stable27745-file payload. Its generated records remain inert historical evidence. The new d25e9c3 capsule/document payload is undergoing its own publication validation before only its two derived records are imported. Source/read/artifact limits and all previous controls remain intact. The diagnostic delivery audit has zero known missing carriers, wrong modes or size mismatches, but969 unresolved declarations; complete graph coverage is not claimed.\n\nProduct tests and builds run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work is code/document authoring, orchestration and recoverable backup verification; no paid resources or billing changes. [Hosted verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) preserve exact scopes. All ten complete replacements, every documented feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain open."
}
