{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Install Notes task creation and preserve Archive native diagnostics",
  "body": "Development is paused at Evan's direct October 18 instruction. Automatic follow-ups are paused; the one owned in-progress hosted run39162757907 was cancelled and its uploaded partial evidence was preserved. A backup-only checkpoint preserves the current code, unfinished proposals, source reviews and retained results without installing untested changes. All ten complete replacements, full documented-feature parity and whole-product superiority remain open.\n\nNotes now supports a direct New To-do draft and first-save flow, including duplicate-save prevention, retention of newer drafts, and explicit recovery after a failed refresh. Commit `3c710a31e438af7f1682fc5cf497be4264db35ff` installs the exact seven application images from the independently reviewed R5 experiment into the normal 36-file application. It also installs a separate committed-source acceptance workflow and bounded source proof. Both historical workflows retain their original manual checks and complete before-images; the new workflow replaces their obsolete automatic source contracts.\n\nThe actual installation journal records all 31 source/document changes, all 11 readable before copies, all 31 readable after copies, and independent readback. Recovery tag `rea-notes36-before-install-e655-20261016` preserves the exact previous commit locally and on GitHub. All 17 existing Notes test files and historical receipts remain unchanged. Fresh installed acceptance is pending: 111 selected checks across 21 files, eight real Chromium scenarios, independent source postchecks, the full implemented-suite superset, and all 306 publication controls with exactly 95 artifact roles. Earlier experimental 111/8 and historical installed 92/8 results retain their original source epochs.\n\nBefore installation, [run38938249306](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38938249306) passed all 1,100 implemented-suite checks with zero failures or skips; all 431 uploaded files are readable locally. The older [D24 failure record](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/tree/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full1100-native-metadata-failure-20261016) remains a confirmed 1,098/1,100 result with two Archive native-metadata refusals. Its original child error was discarded, so the historical cause remains unknown. The separate [native diagnostic record](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/tree/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-native-metadata-diagnostic-20261016) passes five unchanged instrumented checks and records six successful callbacks under the unchanged native deadline and assertions. All 78 uploaded members and original raw observations are publicly recoverable. This does not reproduce or diagnose D24, establish a reliability fix, or provide an uninstrumented performance comparison.\n\nThe earlier Archive AES/native-timestamp integration and Notes conversion/completion/due-date/filter work remain included. Publication's historical 208-control records and imported metadata are preserved; source installation leaves both derived metadata files unchanged until fresh verification of the new payload. All product tests and builds run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work is authoring, orchestration and recoverable backups. All ten full replacements, every documented feature, and whole-product superiority remain open. See [verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md)."
}
{
  "base": "main",
  "head": "codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015",
  "draft": true,
  "title": "Integrate Archive AES and Notes tasks; diagnose native metadata failures",
  "body": "Archive gains AES 7Z, encrypted-header handling and native Windows timestamps. Notes gains saved-note conversion to and from to-dos, completion/reopening, due dates and filters, while retaining drafts, JEX records and resources. Both integrations install exact independently reviewed sources with recoverable before/after journals and pushed pre-installation Git tags.\n\nThe latest full repeat38933603615 passes1,100/1,100 with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos on089cb23; all431 uploaded members are readable locally. The prior d24 full38932318510 remains an unresolved1,098/1,100 result: two Archive ZIP-creation groups refuse native Windows metadata. All798 census entries and374 snapshots match the earlier89e successful source bytes. The original transport error was discarded, so its15-second deadline is a hypothesis rather than an established cause. The complete431-member failure record is now publicly recoverable in results/cloud-full1100-native-metadata-failure-20261016. Commit e655fd9 adds an independently reviewed cloud diagnostic that runs the same two unchanged test files/five groups, preserving the original native command/deadline and observing redacted native callback status. Actualrun38938239800 passes all five instrumented checks, with six successful native calls, all70 source objects stable and all78 uploaded files readable. It does not reproduce or identify the earlier failure, establish a reliability fix or provide an uninstrumented performance comparison. Permanent portable result filing is being prepared. Application source and test assertions are unchanged. Archive161/6 and installedNotes92/8 remain separate source-qualified campaigns, never added to full-suite counts.\n\nDirect New to-do creation is a separately verified source experiment. Corrected run38930449217 passes111/111 finite checks and8/8 Chromium scenarios; all1,108 uploaded members have readable recoverable local copies. The complete portable artifacts, raw evidence and independent reviews are public at [R5 experiment evidence](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/tree/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/products/rea-studio/results/notes-new-todo-r5-cloud-pass-20261016), committed in d24db80. A source-identical d24 repeat38932306725 also passes111/8 with another complete1,108-member backup. This experiment is not yet installed in the normal32-file Notes application; a separate36-file installation proposal is being authored and must receive source review and fresh committed-source acceptance. Installation is held while the actual Archive full-suite failures are investigated.\n\nThe earlier New to-do failure remains failed107/111 and7/8, with all1,110 members and original observers publicly recoverable in results/notes-new-todo-first-failure-20261016. The narrow runtime correction restores notebook actions during Save while retaining task-operation ownership; strict test corrections compare consistent metadata epochs and strengthen exact raw-byte no-change assertions. No failed receipt is relabelled as a pass. Original Joplin helper comparisons remain separate from full database/GUI behavior; provisional desktop persistence has not been executed.\n\nLatest exact-d24 publication run38932318654 passes208 source controls, both root write/recheck phases and963 syntax checks. Its28,806-file /1,364,428,861-byte payload stays stable; the complete92-file artifact and all56 decoded Notes proof objects are readable locally. Its two exact derived metadata files are independently reviewed, imported with all four before/after contents backed up, and committed in089cb23. Fresh089c run38933603624 also passes208/963 and both phases, with a complete92-file backup and56 decoded proof sources; canonical payload and manifest exactly match the imported records. No repeat import is needed for observation clocks. Historical receipts remain bound to their original sources. Both earlier publication failures and all historical source identities remain intact. Vault Empty Recycle Bin remains a separate uninstalled233-check experiment with4 KeePass library comparisons.\n\nBuilds and product tests run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work is lightweight authoring, orchestration and recoverable backup verification. No paid resources or billing changes. [Verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md) retain exact source attribution and limitations. All ten complete replacements, every documented feature and whole-product quality comparisons remain open."
}
