ecovery-20261015/products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-native-metadata-diagnostic-20261016) passes five unchanged instrumented checks and records six successful callbacks under the unchanged native deadline and assertions. All 78 uploaded members and original raw observations are publicly recoverable. This does not reproduce or diagnose D24, establish a reliability fix, or provide an uninstrumented performance comparison.\n\nThe earlier Archive AES/native-timestamp integration and Notes conversion/completion/due-date/filter work remain included. Publication's historical 208-control records and imported metadata are preserved; source installation leaves both derived metadata files unchanged until fresh verification of the new payload. All product tests and builds run on verified GitHub-hosted Windows. Local work is authoring, orchestration and recoverable backups. All ten full replacements, every documented feature, and whole-product superiority remain open. See [verification details](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/blob/codex/rea-cloud-recovery-20261015/CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md)."
}
