{
  "schema": "rea-hosted-browser-case-independent-source-review/v1",
  "reviewer": "/root/checkpoint_recovery",
  "status": "case-sources-ready-for-hosted-attempt",
  "scope": "Read-only source review of the12 finite Flow/Vault browser cases, configuration and roster. The acquisition/collector/workflow is outside this case review and still needs its own review.",
  "spec": "work/hosted-browser-flow-vault-20261015/candidate/products/rea-studio/browser-tests/flow-vault.spec.mjs",
  "specSHA256": "142e3fda1f65fadfaab1eefb105844a62935a665f4dcd02c57146b6c7f11756e",
  "caseCount": 12,
  "blockers": [],
  "resolvedFindings": [
    "The initial held Flow Save/export cases attempted Playwright fill while the application disables the textarea until the held response returns, producing a dependency deadlock. The author replaced both with an explicit real-browser programmatic value/input-event mutation, asserts the control is actually disabled, records ordinaryUserTyping:false and renamed both case/roster labels to disclose that adversarial bypass. No active application source changed."
  ],
  "observations": [
    "The eight Flow groups cover actual CRLF/bareCR/LF import-save-deploy-download bytes, dirty-deploy transport refusal, retained newer draft after a real committed Save, suppressed export for a changed draft, detached-control scrubbing on disposal and actual SVG pointer drag/static-link metadata. The actual download helper saves and reads file bytes and records their relative evidence path and identity.",
    "The four Vault groups cover committed Create and Save with newer drafts across a held final list, dirty entry/group action refusals and disposal after committed Create. The fixture is generated by current candidate KDBX code and disclosed as synthetic, with no original-product execution. Pending group fields remain editable; only the mutation button is disabled.",
    "The timing gates first fetch an actual successful unchanged host response and retain its body identity; only delivery is delayed. Observed committed values are checked separately. The tests do not manufacture success response bodies. Each gate is released in fixture cleanup, awaited with a deadline, and the owned server is closed even if capture fails.",
    "The configuration fixes one Chromium worker, no retries, forbidOnly, finite per-case/global deadlines and a fixed observed browser version. The roster matches the12 authored names after the correction. Real browser failures/page errors/unexpected console errors remain failures."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The spec has not been executed locally or by this reviewer. Source correctness does not establish real browser availability, selector success, pass counts or actual cleanup outcomes.",
    "Two disabled-control draft changes are explicitly adversarial programmatic browser mutations, not ordinary user typing. Their real HTTP/DOM checks must retain that distinction in later summaries.",
    "Acceptance is limited to these12 source-bound groups. It does not establish the full Flow/Vault feature scope, original GUI parity, Archive acceptance, comparative quality or a full-suite result."
  ],
  "localBrowserExecutions": 0,
  "localTests": 0,
  "localBuilds": 0,
  "localSyntaxExecutions": 0,
  "reviewerSourceEdits": 0,
  "activeApplicationEdits": 0
}
