## Current Flow/Vault real-browser evidence

The [hosted Flow/Vault browser run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-browser-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **12/12 finite Chromium cases**, with zero failures, skips or retries, on unmodified tested merge `f138ee5a`, separate from PR head `dc0fce2b`. It verifies three real downloads byte for byte and records twelve screenshots, six real-response timing holds and two explicitly programmatic probes of disabled Flow controls; the latter are not ordinary user typing. All 326 captured source identities stayed exact and their snapshots remain in the verified complete local backup. The public capsule retains every non-source artifact file, the raw downloads and viewable PNG evidence. No original product runs occurred. These results do not establish Archive browser, full-suite, browser-matrix, full-product or comparative acceptance; counts from different campaigns are not added.

Run `38814582306` used the normal shared host with owned random loopback/data fixtures, Playwright `1.64.1`, Chromium revision `1248` / `156.0.8078.4`, one worker and zero retries. Six timing holds delayed responses fetched from the actual host; no handler response was mocked. Two Flow cases intentionally set a disabled textarea value and dispatch an input event in the browser, and their observations explicitly record `ordinaryUserTyping=false`. Vault inputs are synthetic KDBX fixtures generated by the current candidate; no original KeePass GUI or library was executed. Twelve owned server closures were observed. Each case recorded the expected auxiliary favicon 404; unexpected browser errors were zero.

The browser capsule preserves all 42 non-source artifact files plus the complete wrapper job log, public control-plane responses, local backup attestation, backup reader and preservation collector: 50 logical roles and 46 inert objects. Twelve screenshot roles map to eleven native `.png` objects because the LF and CRLF screenshots have identical bytes. All three actual raw download files are retained. Only the 326 active `source/` snapshot payloads are omitted publicly; their paths, sizes, SHA256 identities and before/after inventories remain public, while the complete 368-file readable evidence backup is verified locally. The artifact ZIP SHA256 is `d5e9e98f0924d74946167f603609bcc54baa01f8860dec449e2b2125d781900d`. No browser, product, build or test executed locally while collecting and filing this evidence.

