# Hosted verification and finite experimental evidence

## Latest verified follow-up

The reviewed **Notes task-editing sources are installed and pass fresh committed-source checks**. The [finite job](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-installed-finite-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **92/92 groups across 17 fixed files**, including 23 new groups, and separately records 20 released Joplin helper comparisons. The [browser job](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-installed-browser-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **8/8 real Chromium cases**, with four genuine successful-response holds, two byte-exact downloads, eight screenshots and complete owned cleanups, and one actual HTTP 400 conflict followed by explicit retry. Run `38917424088` tests committed `362bda055ac4cf7201b2d6a75a2b30dc6fedb578` with zero source overlays. Both jobs authenticate all 32 Notes files, eight after-image pins and 27 dependencies before and after execution; independent postchecks pass. Complete 449-file and 495-file local backups are readable, and their exact public portable ZIPs retain every uploaded role. The first readback-tool CRLF extraction failure and both reader versions remain preserved; no product rerun was needed. Native JEX readback retains six unchanged serialized records and the exact binary resource. No original full application or GUI execution is claimed. The [actual installation journal](products/rea-studio/results/notes-todo-installed-20261016/installation-receipt.json) retains its then-pending acceptance wording and all source recovery pins; older experimental results remain separate. The broader implemented suite now passes as recorded below; the 208-control publication replay remains pending.

The [fresh full implemented-suite run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-installed-full1100-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **1,100/1,100 groups with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos** in [run `38917433182`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38917433182), testing actual merge `6c3c4ecad2c60c55eddd8909c0c8d46acf647137` for branch head `362bda05`. All 796 census identities remain stable; 369 eligible committed sources match Git, with exactly three explicit Archive oracle-test loader/helper targets composed. Application runtime and Notes sources have no overlays. All seven eligible Notes after-images, all 17 Notes test files, the 23 authored task groups and 20 separately counted released-helper comparisons are authenticated within this run. The Notes README is outside this verifier's eligible source census; the focused installed jobs authenticate it separately. All five same-attempt prerequisite receipts and the separate oracle-source postcheck pass. The complete 429-file local backup is readable; its exact public outer ZIP retains all 372 source snapshots and every other uploaded byte, while all 57 nonsource roles are also directly retained. The separate 92 finite groups, eight browser cases, 161 Archive groups and overlapping three bounds groups are never added to1,100. This verifies implemented contracts; every documented feature and whole-product superiority remain unproven.

The [first installed-Notes publication failure and reviewed correction](products/rea-studio/results/notes-historical-id-string-correction-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) preserve all 85 uploaded files, the exact outer artifact ZIP and all 56 decoded Notes source-envelope payloads. Run `38917432854` stopped in its first named migration control: zero controls passed and zero root phases started. The historical Notes finite manifest stores its run and artifact IDs as strings; two reader assertions incorrectly required numbers. The correction asserts the exact two historical strings and refreshes their existing module/producer pins. It changes no application source, historical record, control count, envelope table or read limit. Independent review passes; a fresh hosted replay must establish all 208 controls and both root phases before current derived metadata can be accepted.

The **corrected installed Archive epoch** now passes [161/161 finite checks](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-installed-corrected-bounds-finite-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json), a separate overlapping repeat of its three bounds groups, and [6/6 real Chromium scenarios](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-installed-corrected-bounds-browser-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) in run `38911241646` on committed `016ecd175c0700d1a94d5219af6719989a4a6e45`. All 62 Archive files and 21 current target pins match Git; the single corrected test is explicit and the other 20 target identities are unchanged. Both independent postchecks pass. Complete 470-file finite and 474-file browser backups are readable; the exact public portable ZIPs retain every uploaded source snapshot and all other evidence. Native ZIP/7Z structural readback authenticates three archives, five byte-exact restores and six PNGs, with zero browser downloads. The three bounds groups already belong to the 161 selection and are never added as new coverage. The [independent capsule review](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-installed-corrected-bounds-independent-review-20261016.json) preserves the separate review findings.

The [corrected full implemented-suite replay](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-corrected-full-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **1,077/1,077 groups with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos** in [run `38911252546`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38911252546), testing actual merge `b7bb3010fa7f08a45bef8758515f5fbef5566917` for branch head `016ecd17`. All 789 census identities remain stable; 363 unaffected eligible sources match Git and the three oracle-test loader/helper targets are explicitly composed. Application runtime sources are not overlaid. The corrected bounds file is authenticated in the same attempt's Git baseline, executed selection, census and snapshot. All five same-attempt prerequisites and the separate three-target postcheck pass. The separate bsdtar version smoke counts one original process and zero candidate comparisons; independent DLL loading is not claimed. The complete local backup retains all 423 uploaded files, including 366 active snapshots. The public capsule retains every other 57 artifact role plus raw API/log/reader evidence and exact omitted snapshot identities. Earlier failures, predecessor passes and the original installation journal remain unchanged.

The [164-control publication replay](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-publication-164-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) separately passes both root phases, 953 syntax checks and stable **27,745-file / 1,312,337,913-byte** payload verification in run `38911251888` on the same tested merge. All 91 artifact files have readable local backups. Its generated records remain inert evidence; this later capsule/document payload requires fresh publication validation before only its two derived metadata files may be imported. These finite results establish the corrected implemented Archive epoch. The later Notes installation and fresh focused checks are recorded above; Vault Empty Bin remains experimental, and all ten complete-product and comparative gates remain open.

The [Archive browser follow-up](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-browser-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes all six real Chromium scenarios in run `38826463567`, with zero failures, skips, retries or flaky cases. Three archives and five restored files retain their exact bytes. This remains a 21-target ephemeral experiment; it is not installed in the production application. The product has no archive download UI, and this run records zero browser downloads and zero original-product executions.

The exact reviewed 21 Archive after-images have subsequently been [installed in the application source](products/rea-studio/results/archive-aes-installed-20261016/installation-receipt.json), including AES 7Z handling and native Windows source metadata. The actual journal preserves every before/after identity, the independent reviews and a pre-installation Git tag; it records no local product execution. The [installed-source workflow](.github/workflows/archive-installed-cloud.yml) passes [161/161 finite checks across 13 fixed files](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-installed-finite-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) and [six real Chromium scenarios](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-installed-browser-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) in separate jobs of run `38905573441`, testing committed source `5ff0a2fcd99ae2447311780a39688c554fc8fb2b` with no source overlays. All 62 Archive files and 21 after-images match Git before and after both jobs; separate source postchecks pass. The browser job preserves three created archives, five byte-exact restored files and six PNGs, with zero downloads. The finite job separately retains 63 original-helper invocation records across 29 vectors; these are not a count of every original process across the 13 files. Complete local backups contain 466 finite-job and 471 browser-job readable files. Both public capsules retain every non-source artifact file, raw API/log evidence and exact identities for source snapshots omitted publicly. The 156-control publication epoch subsequently passes as recorded below. A later corrected test source requires its own new acceptance. The earlier experimental receipts keep their original uninstalled status.

The [Flow/Vault cleanup follow-up](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-browser-cleanup-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes all twelve real Chromium scenarios in run `38826470332`, with three byte-exact downloads. All twelve cases record drained requests, closed contexts and closed owned servers, with no unexpected errors. This verifies the corrected test-fixture cleanup for these cases; the precise cause of the earlier close timeout remains unproven. Both capsules preserve every uploaded non-source evidence role and identify all omitted source snapshots; complete readable local backups include those snapshots.

The full implemented suite also passes 1,048/1,048 with zero failures or skips in run [38826470337](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38826470337), testing actual merge `a89735ac1dd1dc0d39f1aeb7f71c1ff0b0ef4ac1` and the disclosed three-file oracle-test overlay. All 774 census identities remain stable; the complete local backup contains 409 readable files, including 352 active source snapshots. Artifact `12015467865` has SHA256 `ee9a6760f78f58d031e83a01cc1623c70d7da81b84094161e1bbe0b84dbdc28b`. This later repeat does not replace the earlier public full-pass receipt.

The [Notes task experiment](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-todo-first-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes **92/92 checks across all 17 Notes test files**, including all 23 new groups, in run `38903252258` on branch source `1d6fd83d6e40453e6db96420de15baf7eca50fa0` plus eight explicit experimental source targets. Twenty comparisons against two authenticated released Joplin 3.6.14 helpers are counted separately: sixteen conversions and four completion transitions. Actual HTTP module bytes, persistence after restart, JEX/resource retention and held-response DOM checks pass. All 779 census identities remain stable; 350 unaffected active sources match Git and the independent eight-target postcheck passes. The complete local backup contains 408 readable files, including 357 active snapshots. This extends saved-note task operations; due dates are metadata and do not provide alarms. Real browser acceptance, installation and whole-product comparisons remain open.

The [first Notes browser run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-notes-todo-browser-first-pass-20261016/README.md) passes **8/8 real Chromium cases**, with zero skips, retries or flaky outcomes, in run `38908759571` on committed `f61cb2ee1969b5fc4059f4e20961526d0594c519` plus the exact eight-target Notes experiment. Four unchanged real-response holds, a genuine revision-conflict HTTP 400 and explicit retry, two actual JEX/resource downloads, eight screenshots and all eight owned cleanups are verified. Both independent source postchecks pass; all 383 eligible sources stay stable, and an independent audit matches 376 other sources to the tested Git blobs, seven eligible Notes after-images and the separately pinned README. The complete 467-file artifact, including all source snapshots, is retained locally and in the public capsule's exact portable ZIP, with all 84 other artifact members also recoverable as direct roles. Native TAR and independent backup TAR parsing confirm eight JEX entries, six unchanged original serialized records and the exact binary resource. The backup reader's README naming correction is preserved separately and caused no product rerun. The [source contract](products/rea-studio/experiments/notes-todo-browser/SOURCE-CONTRACT.md.snapshot) retains its original proposal status. Notes installation, original GUI/full-product comparison and every remaining requirement stay open; this browser run adds zero original helper executions.

The [Vault Empty Recycle Bin follow-up](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38903252563) passes **233/233 checks across all 45 selected Vault files**, with zero failures or skips. Four actual released-library child operations, assembly loads, `DeleteAllObjects` calls and comparisons pass, counted separately from the test groups. Save/reopen retains the raw timestamps and observed KDBX 4.1-to-4.0 header change; its expected projection uses the authenticated original writer's exact whole-second serialization rule. No fuzzy tolerance or raw-clock rewrite is used. All 780 census identities remain stable, and the complete local backup contains 416 readable files, including 358 active snapshots. This is an uninstalled experiment, with production and browser acceptance still open.

The [earlier failed follow-ups](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-followup-6301492-20261015) and [failed Flow/Vault browser run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-browser-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) remain separate, immutable evidence. The publication reader now routes explicitly identified historical requirement sources through its existing closed identity resolver; current installed sources remain mandatory, unknown named identities refuse, and no capability registry or behavioral receipt is rewritten. All 92 reader controls and both root phases pass in run `38828050485`; its producer nevertheless fails because two source-only receipts contain fresh invocation times. The [comparison correction](products/rea-studio/results/publication-repeat-clock-correction-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) adds 18 controls and preserves both raw failed receipts. Only three named observation clocks are projected after exact ISO, ordering and observed-phase-bound checks; all other fields remain deeply equal. Its [first hosted replay](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38903745255) passes all 110 controls, both root phases and final payload stability on actual merge `911104a0e02045ca973d1cf493c2cbb9ef9eaa51`. Its complete 64-file backup is verified. New Archive integration and evidence files require their own current-payload validation before derived metadata is imported. No generated metadata from a failed producer is imported. None of these results establishes every documented feature or whole-product superiority.

The first installed-epoch publication run `38905581634` stops at its first control because an old Archive receipt's exact browser status is the string `pending`, while the reader incorrectly requires `false`. The [preserved failure and source correction](products/rea-studio/results/archive-historical-browser-pending-correction-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) retain that immutable receipt, three reader before-images and all eight non-source artifact roles. The correction separately asserts the exact historical string and retains the other seven strict false assertions, all 156 controls and existing read/artifact limits. That failed run passed zero controls and started zero root phases. The [new hosted replay](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-publication-156-pass-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) passes all 156 controls, both root phases and stable 27,485-file payload verification in run `38907053651`, testing merge `f0f35c1895065eab9dd4bf0f8e4fda51a0bb3a5e` for branch head `2e17c4b`. All 91 artifact files have readable local backups; all 15 non-source artifact roles are preserved publicly, including both raw root stdout/stderr pairs, controls and inert generated metadata. A separate repeat `38907306502` also passes for the later `6af30ba` payload of 27,560 files. Neither result imports metadata into subsequent changed payloads or establishes behavioral feature acceptance.

The first broader suite on installed Archive source, [run `38905581957`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38905581957), fails **one of 1,077 groups**: 1,076 pass with zero skips, cancellations or todos. The malformed-properties fixture removes its first byte, which can accidentally describe another valid AES property sequence; that path reaches a folder CRC refusal instead of the expected properties refusal. The precise random byte was not logged, so its value is inferred from the decoder path. The complete 422-file backup preserves all 365 active snapshots, raw output and stable 788-file census. The frozen 13-file finite selection also contains this predecessor test; its earlier passes and a later old-fixture 1,077/1,077 repeat do not resolve the known probabilistic defect. The [reviewed correction](products/rea-studio/results/archive-aes-properties-fixture-correction-20261016/preservation-manifest.json) retains the exact properties-refusal assertion, truncates the final byte while preserving the declared length, and adds deterministic `EF`/`FE` valid-leading-drop counterexamples inside the same three groups. Runtime parsing, the historical 21-target bundle, old receipts and installation journal remain unchanged. One closed named test transition authenticates the corrected current file and both historical/current snapshots. The extra targeted three-group phase repeats a subset of finite 161; counts are never added as extra coverage. Fresh finite, browser, full-suite and 164-control publication results remain required; the eight additional source controls retain all earlier checks and bounds.

The [later Flow/Vault and collector-control run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-controls-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **282/282 finite contract checks with zero skips** on revision `a2e0aa7`, using a standard GitHub-hosted `windows-2022` runner and Node `24.16.0`. Its 764-file census stayed exact during execution; all 342 active source snapshots, raw logs and synthetic control evidence have verified readable local backups. Four synthetic collector controls pass separately. The [initial finite run](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-flow-vault-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) retains its earlier 282/762/340 epoch on `14e4859`; the historical 937/737 development checkpoint retains its own sources and receipt. Later runner/census changes need their own actual result. The later full-suite attempt failed; the finite current Flow/Vault browser pass and Windows correction experiment are recorded below. Complete ten-application and comparative acceptance remain pending.

After opening the recovery pull request, the workflow runs for relevant pushes to `main`, pull requests, and manual dispatch, avoiding both a branch-push run and a pull-request run for the same update. Its three external actions are pinned to complete Git commit IDs. It requests only repository-content read access, retains no checkout credential, creates no cache or paid resource, and has a 30-minute job deadline. GitHub supplies `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true`; the bootstrap also requires `CI=true`, `RUNNER_ENVIRONMENT=github-hosted`, Windows and the exact Node version before doing any acquisition. It refuses normal local execution.

## Original verification inputs

`products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-flow-vault.mjs` acquires verification inputs on the hosted runner:

- Flow: the committed oracle package and lock files populate ignored `.local/flow-original`. The lock SHA256 is authenticated, the selected Node-RED packages are pinned to `5.0.8` and the test helper to `0.3.6`, and the runner's npm installs with `ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund`. The existing tests independently authenticate selected original source bytes.
- Vault: the recorded KeePass `2.61.1` portable ZIP is fetched from the JiriSko GitHub mirror. The exact archive size and publisher-matching SHA256 recorded in `projects/07-keepass/artifact-manifest.json` are required before extraction. The complete portable package stays under ignored `.local/keepass-original`; the extracted `KeePass.exe` size and SHA256 are required before its path is exported to the suite. The transport is a third-party mirror. OpenPGP verification and reproducible-build verification are not claimed.

Original packages and executable files are never included in the public source or evidence artifact. The application does not import the bootstrap or downloaded verification programs. The workflow does not start an original product service.

`windows-tar-readiness.json` separately records the runner's `System32/tar.exe` SHA256 against the exact historical bsdtar oracle pin. A mismatch leaves the full development suite's Archive prerequisites unresolved; it does not fail this finite Flow/Vault acquisition. The readiness check reads bytes without executing tar. Portable ZIP extraction separately uses runner-provided tar, and the resulting original executable is authenticated.

## Receipts and recoverable evidence

Each GitHub run attempt gets a separate evidence directory under `RUNNER_TEMP`, outside the Studio source census. The bootstrap writes `prerequisite-acquisition.json` with running and terminal acquisition state. The test runner writes its own attempt receipt, streaming raw stdout/stderr, source inventories and snapshots, and events. Its exact selected tests and source-stability results, when completed, determine the scope of the result. Acquisition success alone is not a test pass.

The Flow/Vault workflow includes four synthetic collector controls through `verify-cloud-controls.mjs`: an assertion failure after an early output marker, a deliberate skipped test, an owned source-file change, and a hanging test stopped by a one-second deadline. Each uses an isolated synthetic Git repository and visibly fake prerequisite receipt under `RUNNER_TEMP`. All four controls pass in run `38805892204` on `a2e0aa7`, preserving each intended failed attempt, early raw output and terminal evidence. They execute synthetic tests only; their counts stay separate from the 282 product checks. Run `38803745286` predates this addition and establishes no collector-control result. Acceptance of later collector changes requires a separate result.

The later public capsule preserves every non-source-tree evidence file, including raw logs and all four controls' receipts, events and source manifests. It omits **402 source-snapshot payloads: 342 application snapshots and 60 synthetic snapshots**. Their exact identities remain in the preserved source inventories/manifests and omission list. The complete ZIP and all 463 readable files, including those omitted payloads, remain verified in the local backup. This capsule does not claim complete public source capture.

The workflow always attempts to package available evidence as a portable ZIP and upload it with one-day retention. The complete compressed ZIP is capped at **15 MiB**. A larger ZIP fails the storage gate and uploads only a clearly marked, bounded diagnostic fallback; that fallback is not a complete evidence backup. No dependency or original-program cache is uploaded.

Download the actual artifact contents promptly into the established authorized local work destination. Retain the portable evidence ZIP and readable extracted files; record the GitHub run URL, source commit, run ID and attempt. Verify the terminal receipt, raw-log readability, listed source identities and the copied prerequisite receipt. Keep acquisition, tests, browser checks and the full development checkpoint as distinct results. A URL, expiring GitHub artifact or placeholder alone does not establish a recoverable local backup. Failed, cancelled and incomplete attempts remain separate historical evidence; never complete an older attempt by substituting a rerun's files.

Artifact storage is shared with the account's other repositories and runs. The one-job, one-day, 15 MiB configuration bounds this workflow's requested storage; it does not assert available account quota. GitHub-hosted public-repository execution is the intended supported environment. Do not change billing, select a paid runner or increase the artifact budget without authorization.

## Separate Archive experiment

[The Archive workflow](.github/workflows/archive-aes-cloud.yml) prepares a separate hosted experiment from the inert `products/rea-studio/experiments/archive-aes` bundle. [The first attempt38805892328](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-composition-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) failed baseline source-census qualification on `a2e0aa7`, before any overlay transition, original acquisition or test execution. Its two artifact files, local backup attestation and job log remain preserved as that failed epoch.

[The earlier attempt38806502120](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-metadata-failure-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) composed the overlay on baseline `9970992`, acquired the original verification inputs and executed the thirteen selected test files: **160 checks, 154 passes, six failures and zero skips**. Its 776-file census remained stable during execution; the separate post-run source check also passed. Six failures concern DOS short-path versus long-path aliases in hosted Windows source metadata. This attempt remains a separate failed epoch.

This failure capsule retains all 18 non-source artifact files, including raw output, composition/acquisition receipts and both observation files, plus the job log and local backup attestation. Its **354 omitted `verification/source/` snapshot payloads** remain in the complete, byte-verified 372-file readable local backup. Their identities and source manifests remain public. Source stability and the failed test outcome are separate recorded facts; the full Archive and ten-application suites remain open.

[The earlier attempt38808025295](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-prerequisites-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) ran on the composed overlay based on `b15d166`: **161 checks, 155 passes, six failures and zero skips**, with a stable 779-file census. Its path-spelling diagnostic records `differentSpelling=true` for the hosted short-name temporary path and its long-name form. This failed epoch remains preserved separately from the later literal-path correction.

That capsule preserves all 32 non-source artifact files, including every prerequisite receipt and acquisition log, the candidate raw output and both observations, plus the job log and backup attestation. Its **357 omitted source-snapshot payloads** remain in the complete, verified 389-file local backup. Their identities and manifests remain public. Its prerequisite phases passed separately from its failed candidate result.

[The later attempt38808918976](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-archive-aes-finite-pass-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) passes **161/161 finite experimental checks**, with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos, after the literal-path correction. Its actual tested Git baseline is merge `7d5bde3fb94e3383e6d85e50e7d567516cc6202c` at `refs/pull/1/merge`; PR head `aeb62e6` is a separate identity. The composition manifest SHA256 is `4fe7b114341199fa31d5553ffb3505db0e3427337ea8c72c637a8d5a3501a042`. The 779-file composed census remained stable, and the separate post-run source check passed. All three ZIP, plain-7Z and encrypted-7Z path diagnostics retain `differentSpelling=true`, showing `RUNNER~1` paths resolving to `runneradmin` paths while the physical timestamp checks pass.

The successful finite capsule preserves all **32 non-source artifact files**, including metadata, prerequisite receipts and logs, raw test output and both observations, plus the job log, local backup attestation and preservation collector. Its **357 source-snapshot payloads** are explicitly omitted publicly and remain in the complete, byte-verified **389-file** readable local backup. Their exact paths, sizes and digests remain in the public omission list and source manifests. Finite experimental contracts pass; production installation remains false, and browser acceptance, the full Archive scope and the full ten-application suite remain pending.

`compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs` authenticates the committed baseline and selected experimental source bytes, then composes an explicit overlay in the ephemeral hosted checkout. The changes include selected AES/container behavior and source timestamp collection. `composition.json` records the baseline Git commit, approved source identities and the composed source census; the test collector receives it through `--overlay-manifest`. Each tested source identity combines its actual baseline commit and composition manifest. A stable before/after census describes that attempt's composed bytes and does not equate them with the Git baseline. The composition is confined to the experimental hosted checkout; production installation remains false.

Original 7-Zip acquisition, overlay composition, execution and post-run checks produce separate evidence. Future experimental results must retain their actual run ID, raw logs, exact sources and local backups. Their counts remain separate from the finite 282 Flow/Vault checks, the four synthetic collector controls and the historical 937 development checks. The experiment leaves the full ten-application suite and comparative acceptance pending.

## Remaining broader verification work

In the successful finite run38808918976, `bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs` acquired the exact Microsoft `tar.exe` and adjacent `archiveint.dll` pair from official image endpoints. `verify-cloud-bsdtar.mjs` separately recorded **one successful original `--version` process**, with zero candidate comparisons. These prerequisite phases also passed in earlier run38808025295. The EXE retains the historical digest; the paired DLL has a newly explicit identity. Loaded module paths were not independently observed, and this result does not establish which DLL the earlier EXE-only historical run loaded. The reviewed paired-image test-loader overlay was used in the completed but failed full replay below; it does not establish full-suite acceptance.

`bootstrap-cloud-development.mjs` also completed acquisition in that run: **four Automation archives and 4,350 authenticated source files, 202 routing-cache files, three Sketch assets, and two Restic assets (archive and executable)**, with zero skipped prerequisites. Its bounded acquisition logs and receipt are preserved. Automation's acquisition command initializes released original modules for integrity checking; that disclosed initialization is separate from comparative tests. This bootstrap ran zero comparative test processes and started zero original application services.

Linux coverage is deferred. An identical Linux certificate would be misleading because current original-product comparisons use Windows PowerShell and Windows executables. The existing full development verifier additionally requires every prerequisite and zero skipped tests; this workflow's finite receipt cannot replace it.

The later successful full-suite replay below used a clean hosted checkout, repeated prerequisite authentication, the reviewed paired-image test-loader composition and a complete zero-skip passing result. Acquired inputs and one version smoke do not establish that acceptance. The finite Flow/Vault browser pass below covers its twelve declared cases; broader browser and independent checkpoint acceptance remain separate work. All earlier receipts preserve their original source attribution.

The [full current-suite attempt 38810678336](products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full-suite-failed-20261015/preservation-manifest.json) is a completed failure: 1,042 tests, 1,024 passes, 18 failures and no skips/cancellations/todos. It tested actual merge `abcac0b2f7905838198bdaa2e11461ac52cdb75e`, separately from PR head `6f89a09`, with exactly three reviewed oracle-loader test sources composed and zero application-runtime changes. All prerequisites and the separate source postcheck passed; 770 eligible sources stayed stable. The public capsule retains 60 logical records/41 objects, including all non-source artifact files and raw wrapper output. Its 348 omitted active source payloads remain in the complete verified readable local backup. One Editor assertion observes canonical versus short root spelling; 17 Sync WebDAV cases stop at the alias guard. The later 47-check hosted experiment below verifies the source-reviewed candidate corrections separately. They were subsequently integrated as exact reviewed source images; the later complete implemented-suite pass is recorded below. Passing 1,024 checks does not turn this failed run into acceptance.

