    "finding": "The original strict roster comparison used full repository paths on one side and Studio-relative paths on the other, so proof() would reject before any campaign.",
    "correction": "Exactly one literal now removes only the fixed products/rea-studio/ prefix from current test paths before comparing the unchanged bundle roster. All ten other candidate files and the API document are byte-identical. No test or assertion was removed."
  },
  "review": [
    "Read the complete helper body, API contract, declaration semantic fields and role tables, authoring source and data-audit source. Read the complete one-literal R2 delta and independently reconstructed the final helper from preserved R1 bytes. The corrected path domains compare equal as data for the exact21-file roster; no helper import, syntax check or local test was performed.",
    "Independently checked the exact11 candidate paths, all before/after identities, seven app images equal to the previously reviewed and actually successful R5 images, all17 old test files unchanged, both full historical workflow snapshots equal to immutable d24 Git, and the exact36 app/21-test source set.",
    "The declaration lists precisely the other59 fixed proof rows, equal to the reviewed R5 composed source closure with the experimental workflow removed. Helper externally pins the declaration; combined60 objects total695,900 bytes under64/8MiB/256KiB limits. No declaration/helper/collector self-pin cycle exists. Original model, license, command, review, before-image and after-image inputs remain individually fixed.",
    "All52 legacy proof logical identities exactly match the old producer table, all52 physical paths are distinct, and only client/server/README map to their exact R5 before aliases. The separate four legacy tooling rows match old pins; only the retired installed workflow maps to its complete frozen snapshot. The combined56 logical/physical sets remain unique, and changed roles are explicitly historical.",
    "Hosted guard requires exact Windows/X64 Node24.16.0 repository/run/job/HEAD context, ordinary SHA1 Git blobs and a clean checkout. proof() authenticates all60 inputs to committed Git bytes; authenticateCensus closes the six-directory names against the actual Git tree and excludes no installed target. All34 eligible Notes sources and36 app files remain separately mandatory.",
    "Before/after APIs use distinct committed36 schemas, exact source inputs, same-attempt job identity, before-receipt identity, fresh proof and full census. The CLI performs no installation or composition, records zero product/original/browser executions, captures complete bounded source snapshots before tests, and fails closed if an independent after check cannot reauthenticate the original before census.",
    "The future standalone collector must use value.authentication.sourceAuthentication and these committed-source filenames rather than experimental composition fields. It must retain strict111/21/23+19/20+4+2 and unchanged eight-browser semantics, independently authenticate its12 tooling rows before helper import, Git-bind itself and preserve separate always postchecks. Those unimplemented pieces are outside this subset approval.",
    "Seven app images remain source proposals here. One client component was previously authored by this reviewer and independently reviewed by Notes; this review authenticates its unchanged R5 bytes and independently reviews the new helper/declaration/maps. All prior authorities, failed runs and installed32 receipts remain distinct."
  ],
