  "migrationFindings": [
    "The new declaration is externally pinned and reads exactly59 additional declared objects, yielding60 bounded objects/695900 bytes under64 files/8MiB/256KiB individual limits. The declaration cannot contain its own identity. The21-file roster strips the Studio prefix correctly, seven R5 app identities and17 payloads are mandatory, and the distinct20/4/2 helper comparison counts remain outside group totals.",
    "The historical52 logical and52 physical rows match the complete old fixed object plan. Only client/server/README project to exact current32 before-images. The original52 verifier body is byte-identical and receives a closed legacyRead, never a generic fallback. Four historical tooling rows are explicitly source metadata here; the producer must authenticate their physical56 envelope separately.",
    "The seven current routes precede the older eight: exact R5 current identities return null; exact current32 predecessors return their fixed new before-image alias; exact still-older Notes predecessors continue through the old authenticated route. Unknown identities still throw. The current union is explicitly12 and the historical eight remain separately qualified.",
    "R2 changes only four summary flags. The module authenticates36 named current objects; it does not prove an actual live directory census. That separate hosted helper requirement is explicit. Existing common85/159 and Archive94 group identities/budgets retain their historical scope and are not renamed as an aggregate fresh36 acceptance. No new installed behavior is preclaimed."
  ],
