  "completeCollectorBodyAndWorkflowRead": true,
  "independentSourceDataAudit": {"path": "work/notes36-cloud-r2-independent-source-data-audit-20261016.json", "bytes": 1232, "sha256": "f1a8ab3103902c3b8bc7baf621bf6345ec82a808d786e657a467c127d7d7b7a5"},
  "reviewedHelperApi": {"bytes": 16788, "sha256": "648f28c93ee6f08f93fb6d715e9208f31dd12e8af45097fef01d58161ec2cbe2"},
  "findings": [
    "The new collector authenticates its own actual Git blob and the literal fixed helper before import. It calls the reviewed readInstalled API and obtains authentication.sourceAuthentication from the correct nested object. Current36 mandatory sources, seven installed images/six eligible images and every eligible live census object require exact Git identities with no overlays or excluded targets.",
    "The fixed tooling list is exactly12 unique literal rows matching the authority and actual candidate/helper/declaration/unchanged inputs. Each is below256KiB and the aggregate remains below8MiB. The33324-byte collector self is separate, Git-bound and absent from the12-row table; final publication must independently literal-pin it in the explicit95th-role source slot, avoiding a self-pin cycle.",
    "Child supervision, output bounds, descendant stop handling, complete close/no-interruption assertions and PNG/TAR parsers retain the reviewed R5 implementation. The finite validator differs only by its installation object name and own observation filename; it still requires111/111 across21 fixed files,23+19 named groups and distinct20/4/2 original helper counts. No full original application/database/GUI execution is invented.",
    "All eight real browser validators retain the reviewed R5 body except the equivalent current36 declaration source array. Actual enabled UI behavior, canonical full raw-note identity, three successful plus one failed response holds, two real restored filesystem400 faults, two byte-exact downloads, eight PNG CRCs and owned cleanups remain strict. Native TAR readback still preserves seven original serialized records plus the binary resource before assessing the new task.",
    "The unchanged acquisition validator projects only GITHUB_JOB from the ten-field source execution object to the existing nine-field acquisition receipt. Every other provenance field, package/lock/browser metadata, actual executable identity and child close/no-error outcome remains exact.",
    "The collector always captures/rechecks the active census after execution. The workflow adds independent always-attempted helper source-after for both jobs and a separate browser-postcheck that binds the same attempt/tooling/source-before receipt and current census, even after product failures. Source-verified status is distinct from product acceptance.",
    "The two jobs retain pinned Windows/Node/actions, exact actual checkout, external owned evidence/cache, read-only permissions and2500-file/96MiBraw/8MiBindividual/15MiBZIP bounds. Explicit incomplete fallback cannot earn acceptance. Trigger coverage includes both actual old workflow paths, proof declarations, app/experiment/browser/tooling/shared dependencies. R2 corrects the actual notes-installed workflow name and stale composition step label, changing only the resulting workflow pin inside the collector; R1 stays preserved."
  ],
  "remainingConditions": [
    "This source pair is not an installation or observed current36 pass. Root must review and atomically install the separately frozen app/proof/producer/control/historical-workflow transition, including an actual recoverable source journal.",
    "The collector and workflow explicitly do not authenticate an installation journal and perform no installation. Keep that limitation in public scope rather than treating source proof as installation evidence.",
    "Final producer/control source must preserve all208 prior controls, independently close the proposed current60/12/self and95 artifact roles, retain historical52/56 physical projections, and receive a complete integrated peer before copy.",
    "Fresh installed111/8, the full-suite superset, both independent postchecks and publication evidence with recoverable complete backups remain required. No parity, reliability cure, performance superiority or complete-product acceptance is established by source review."
  ],
