Publication helpers and narrow allowlist additions
-------------------------------------------------
work/stage-flow-vault-publication.mjs is the copied
work/prepare-editor-vault-publication.mjs implementation. It currently requires
branch main, performs git add --all, enumerates staged Git blobs, rejects vendor
carriers except the single exact synthetic native-zip93.zip fixture, regenerates
PUBLICATION-MANIFEST.json and excludes PUBLICATION-MANIFEST.json/VALIDATION.json.
work/publish-flow-vault-checkpoint.mjs similarly assumes main and runs root --write
locally before committing/pushing; its anonymous20-file list includes a prospective
FLOW-LINKS-VAULT-EDIT-MILESTONE.md and flow-vault-combined-20261013 that are absent.
Neither helper is ready for unchanged reuse on this recovery branch.

Prepare a derived reviewed helper with explicit branch/commit and exact intended
paths, hosted manifest generation/root syntax validation, and no automatic main
push. Preserve old helper source and exact transformation. Root/source receipts
must distinguish tested14e4859 from later publication commit. Do not silently
update PUBLICATION.json's branch/main claim or publication receipt before verifying
the actual chosen remote state and anonymously retrieved exact blobs.

The legacy allowed products/rea-studio/ prefix already covers cloud scripts/docs,
the finite capsule and Archive experimental snapshots. Narrowly permit only these
new outside-prefix paths in a derived staging/publishing helper:
  CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md
  .github/workflows/flow-vault-cloud.yml
  .github/workflows/archive-aes-cloud.yml
  scripts/verify-cloud-recovery-records.mjs (only if the proposed module is authored)
Existing README.md, scripts/verify-records.mjs and
scripts/editor-vault-proof-migration.mjs are already permitted by legacy rules.

Inside the broad Studio prefix, enumerate/review the actual intended additions:
  scripts/verify-cloud.mjs
  scripts/bootstrap-cloud-flow-vault.mjs
  scripts/verify-cloud-controls.mjs
  scripts/compose-archive-aes-cloud.mjs
