  experiments/archive-aes/ + the46 exact sourcePayloads named by bundle.json
  results/cloud-flow-vault-20261015/preservation-manifest.json +351 named inert objects
  the already reviewed Flow/Vault installation/proof and source-map destinations.
Do not add a generic .github/ allowance, generic external archive allowance, or
permission for arbitrary experimental files. Reject unexpected deletions/renames,
credentials, vendor executables and full vendor/source archives. Keep existing
single synthetic ZIP exception exactly path+SHA bound; no new binary is published
by the baseline6 correction (those fixtures were already committed).

Keep the root document-link check and all existing credential/vendor exclusions.
Experimental candidate compatibility Markdown remains inert .snapshot text; its
future installed publication-index link is explicitly unfulfilled, not a license
to fabricate an installed proof map. The experimental README's links are ordinary
scope/command documentation.

Proposed hosted validation sequence
-----------------------------------
  1. Author/preserve/review the named root-verifier third transition and finite
     cloud verifier; leave historical receipts immutable.
  2. Generate the intended full publication manifest from reviewed committed/staged
     Git bytes on supported hosted compute; preserve all excluded-record semantics.
  3. Run root publication integrity/syntax validation there and retain success or
     failure with exact source revision. This is source/record validation, not a
     rerun of937 or282 behavior.
  4. Report separate historicalDevelopment937/737, finiteFlowVault282/762/340,
     new fullDevelopmentSuiteAcceptance=false, browser pending and all parity false.
     Collector-control and experimental Archive results require their own actual
     run receipts, including failures, never expected counts substituted as results.
  5. Review the concrete payload/receipt, publish only within the parent's authorized
     branch scope, verify the remote tree and anonymous exact bytes, and retain local
     portable source/evidence backups. Local links alone are not complete backups.

